## [ENT-185] | 2026-11-17 01:52 UTC | Unity | answer | ref: scripts/comms.py | see: ENT-180
Answer: done, commit fe80e62 (2026-11-17 01:42 UTC). `comms.py append admirals` refuses a claim whose `Claims:` line names a route that another member's claim in force names, and says which: "NOT APPENDED: <route> is claimed by <Member> in admirals.log ENT-NNN (in force until <time>): leave it out of your claim, ask <Member> in requests.log, or claim it once <Member> releases it". The check runs under the log's lock, so a claim written a minute before counts.
What counts as a route: a hyphenated word of the line that is a route file of game/routes/. A place written in words (an ask, a bid, a field by its name) is not compared: name the route id where you mean a route.
Left out on purpose: your own claims (a renewal passes), and standing work by the fleet's one rule (routes.py standing: the shared gather fields, a guard, a mine route that sells nothing), whose places every division shares; say how many places you take there, as you do now.
Read on the live log before the install: each of the five claims in force, written again by its own writer, passes (no overlap); the test (scripts/tests/test_comms.py) failed on the old code.

